    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ον </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Alc.</u>
			33
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Tr.</u>
			530
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>Ps.</u>
			51(52).6
		</span></i>, etc. (lyr.): —<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crafty, deceitful, treacherous,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> always of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπεα, τέχνη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				9.282
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.455
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁππότε . . δόλιον περὶ κύκλον
				ἄγωσιν</span> the <i>treacherous</i> circle, i. e. the
			net, <i><span class="en">
				4.792
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆνις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					155
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.82
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλιον ὄμμ᾽ ἔχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					569
				</span></i>
			; epith. of Aphrodite, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				16.116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				238
			</span></i> (lyr.); of Hermes, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				133
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1157
			</span></i>; in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.34.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. χείλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Pr.</u>
					26.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνελεύθερος καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.60
				</span></i>
			 W. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Batr.
					93
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				387.7
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Apamea</span>), <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				9.4
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.35
			</span></i>.</div>
